# Two throws into the pile of 300: hundreds of bodies awake at once, far more than one state
# packet holds. stale_ticks.max is the sender's own promise, not a sync check: it holds with no
# network at all. Its bound is max(4, 30 + ceil(M / N)) ticks; here M is about 300 awake bodies
# and N at least 55 records of a 1000-byte packet (a copy with every rare group), so 36, read
# as 40 with a margin. The stub sends everything every tick and reads 0.
scenario load_overflow
scene load300
seed 31
guests 1
settle 10s

net g1 rtt 80ms jitter 10ms loss 2%

p0 walk load200
p0 grab load200 as a0
p0 wait 300ms
p0 throw 0 0.5 0 speed 12
p1 walk load299
p1 grab load299 as a1
p1 wait 300ms
p1 throw 0 0.5 0 speed 12

expect result a0 granted
expect result a1 granted
expect stale_ticks.max <= 40t
expect agree_at_rest 5cm
expect no_stuck
